    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Dealing with malicious or uncooperative employees requires you to shift from remediation to clear boundaries and consistent enforcement of company policies. Instead of hoping they will change, you must directly document every instance of the specific infraction with dates, times, witnesses, and exactly which policy rule was violated during each interaction. In these severe cases, you often can skip the standard first step of a casual verbal warning if the behavior is immediate, dangerous, or a direct threat to the company's safety or integrity. For such situations, phrase your documentation as a formal statement of fact and immediately move toward expulsion or termination, citing that the conduct was never intended to be tolerated. Always involve HR early in the process to ensure you don't accidentally commit an illegal dismissal.",
